      "writtenOn": "2022-01-12T11:48:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "index won\u0027t change, but eventCache should grow: this loop waits until its size is \u003e\u003d index, and returns the element at index.\n\nThe previous loop:\n\n    for (; index \u003c mEventCache.size(); index++) {\n        EventData e \u003d mEventCache.get(index);\n        return e;\n    }\n\nIs actually an overcomplicated \"if\" statement, since it returns if it enters the loop once. So \"index\" is actually never incremented, and it\u0027s equivalent to:\n\n    if (index \u003c mEventCache.size())",
